[[Lieutenant]] '''Matthew Arliss Mura''' was a [[Bajoran]] [[25th century]] [[Starfleet]] [[operations division]] [[officer]].

== Early life ==
Mura was [[Childbirth|born]] sometime after [[2376]]. ({{PIC|Võx}})

He had a [[Unnamed Bajorans#Mura's son|son]]. ({{PIC|Surrender}})

== Starfleet career ==
=== Tactical officer of the USS ''Titan''-A ===
In [[2401]], Lt. Mura served as the [[tactical officer]] aboard the {{USS|Titan|NCC-80102-A|-A}}. He was on [[bridge]] duty when [[First officer]] [[Commander]] [[Seven of Nine|Hansen]] brought guests [[Admiral]] [[Jean-Luc Picard]] and [[Captain]] [[William T. Riker]] with her and after the ''Titan''-A departed [[Sol Station|spacedock]] on their mission. ({{PIC|The Next Generation}})

=== Tactical officer of the USS ''Enterprise''-G ===
In [[2402]], Mura was assigned to newly rechristened {{USS|Enterprise|NCC-1701-G|-G}} as tactical officer. He was present on the bridge of the ''Enterprise'' when Ensign Crusher reported for duty and the ''Enterprise'' headed out on their [[shakedown|shakedown cruise]].  ({{PIC|The Last Generation}})

